\section{Universal Evolution Operator}

Let the state of the manifold at time \(t\) be
\[
\mathcal{S}(t) = \{ T_i(t), \rho_i(t), \chi_i(t), g_{\mu\nu}^{(i)}(t) \}_{i=1}^N.
\]

Define the evolution operator
\[
\mathcal{E} : \mathcal{S}(t) \mapsto \mathcal{S}(t + \Delta t),
\]
such that
\[
\mathcal{S}(t + \Delta t) = \mathcal{E}[\mathcal{S}(t); \mathcal{L}_{\text{matter}}],
\]
where \(\mathcal{L}_{\text{matter}}\) is a pluggable matter Lagrangian.

Constraint preservation:
\[
\det(g_{\mu\nu}^{(i)}(t)) > 0, \quad
\nabla_\mu J^\mu = 0, \quad
\chi(\mathcal{T}) = \text{const}
\]
for all \(t\), where \(\chi(\mathcal{T})\) is the global Euler characteristic.